{
  "_comment": [
    "Measured on rbe-west, the lane's own remote executors (instance oss), on",
    "2026-10-09: one `bazel test --config=embedded --nocache_test_results",
    "//cmd/bd:bd_embedded_test //cmd/bd:bd_embedded_part2_test` run (race,",
    "`-test.parallel=4`, the 100-shard block split 50+50 over the two targets),",
    "so every top-level TestEmbedded* function ran exactly once. It was taken",
    "after the slowest functions were split into smaller top-level functions",
    "(subtests moved verbatim): the sum of test-seconds fell from ~10.3k",
    "(50 shards, the previous capture) to ~8.1k, partly because each shard now",
    "runs fewer tests at once. The remaining >60s functions are the *Concurrent",
    "stress tests, whose bd subprocesses queue on the workspace's single writer",
    "lock, and fixtures that seed many issues one `bd create` at a time.",
    "",
    "Each value is that top-level test's own <testcase time=...> from Bazel's",
    "generated test.xml, NOT the enclosing <testsuite time=...>: <testsuite",
    "time> is a wall-clock-since-binary-start timestamp that does not isolate a",
    "concurrently-run top-level test's own duration under -test.parallel=4,",
    "while <testcase time> matches the test binary's own `--- PASS: TestX (Ys)`",
    "line. Go adds a parallel test's elapsed time to its duration before it",
    "waits for a parallel slot, so slot wait is not counted.",
    "",
    "The generator packs these with a model of the shard process",
    "(_embedded_shard_manifest_lib.py's pack_concurrent): functions without a",
    "top-level t.Parallel() run one after another, before the parallel ones,",
    "which share -test.parallel=4 slots.",
    "",
    "`seconds_per_init_fallback` is sum(durations) / sum(inits) over every test",
    "here (inits: discover_inits_cost()'s t.Run( count proxy), used only for a",
    "brand-new test with no entry yet.",
    "",
    "These are a relative weight for packing, not an absolute SLA."
  ],
